{
  "$schema": "../quest.schema.json",
  "id": "quest-crate-for-mr-s",
  "title": "The Crate for Mr. S—",
  "summary": "Vane's next crate of relics sits in bay nine of Wendmouth's bonded warehouse, bound for the Gilded Tern and a buyer who signs himself Mr. S—. Inside, under the horn-coins, is a Hornfolk name-stone carved with Horn's mother's name. Take it before the Tern sails.",
  "notes": "Side quest of Wendmouth (bible 3.6, 4.3, 6.1 quest 6; mw-e39.21), optional to the main quest: it writes crate.intercepted and horn.name-stone-held but the main quest reads no harbour fact to advance, and the quest never writes tern.sailed (the main quest does, when Act III begins). Started by whichever lead the player finds first: Nell on bay nine, Mags on the crates, Cray's suspicion of the seal or Quell's collapse. Every route is an optional objective and every resolution names the one it needs, so any class's route counts (route-matrix bay-nine, customs-strongroom, gilded-tern). How the player gets into bay nine (skylight, pick, dockhand's coat, forged stamp, Mage Hand on the seal) is the level's business: it emits crate.bay-opened and the other events when the obstacle is beaten. Wendmouth has no scene yet (follow-up bead), so the event and area objectives complete through completeObjective until then. Each resolution sets crate.method; the Tern sailing first resolves it as 'sailed' and leaves the customs manifest copy obtainable.",
  "givers": ["npc-nell"],
  "startWhen": {
    "kind": "any",
    "of": [
      {
        "kind": "fact",
        "fact": "nell.bay-nine-told"
      },
      {
        "kind": "fact",
        "fact": "mags.crates-confessed"
      },
      {
        "kind": "fact",
        "fact": "cray.bay-nine.suspicion"
      },
      {
        "kind": "fact",
        "fact": "quell.collapsed"
      }
    ]
  },
  "stages": [
    {
      "id": "rumour",
      "text": "Vane's next relic crate is waiting in bay nine of the bonded warehouse to be hoisted aboard the Gilded Tern, and the Tern sails when the trouble up the valley comes to a head. Whatever you do, do it before then.",
